India]\n21: \n22: #### Kolhapuri Chappals\n23: * **Region**: Kolhapur district.\n24: * **Technique**: Hand-crafted, vegetable-dyed leather craft. Stitched with leather cords, no nails used.\n25: * **Recognition**: GI Tagged. [Source: Patent Design and Trademarks Office, India]\n26: \n27: #### Sawantwadi Crafts\n28: * **Region**: Sindhudurg district.\n29: * **Crafts**: Wooden toys, Ganjifa cards (circular playing cards), lacquerware (chess sets, fruits).\n30: * **Current Status**: Struggling but supported by royal family descendants and MTDC.\n31: \n32: #### Pinguli Chitrakatha\n33: * **Region**: Pinguli village, Sindhudurg.\n34: * **Community**: Thakar community.\n35: * **Technique**: Broad leaves/paper paintings depicting Ramayana/Mahabharata, accompanied by oral storytelling (leather puppetry/string puppetry).\n36: * **Status**: Endangered. [SCHOLARLY INTERPRETATION]\n37: \n38: ---\n39: \n40: ### PART 13: Music\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
